   If a number \(n\) can be expressed in its prime factorization form as:
   \[
   n = p_1^{e_1} \times p_2^{e_2} \times \ldots \times p_k^{e_k}
   \]
   where \(p_1, p_2, \ldots, p_k\) are distinct prime factors and \(e_1, e_2, \ldots, e_k\) are their respective positive integer exponents, then the total number of positive divisors \(d(n)\) of \(n\) is given by:
   \[
