### Step 2: Outline the Approach
We can define a function \(f(n)\) that represents the number of ways to write \(n\) as the sum of \(1\text{'s},\) \(2\text{'s},\) and \(4\text{'s}.\) The recurrence relation for this function can be established based on the last number added to the sum:

