   - The total number of ways to distribute \( n \) indistinguishable items (jerseys) into \( k \) distinguishable boxes (teams) is given by the "stars and bars" theorem:
     \[
     \text{Ways} = \binom{n+k-1}{k-1}
     \]
   - We will also need to consider cases where teams do not meet the gender requirement.

### Detailed Calculations

#### Step 1: Total Distributions Without Restrictions
Each team can receive any combination of the 12 jerseys. The total number of ways to distribute 12 indistinguishable jerseys into 3 distinguishable teams is:
\[
\text{Total Ways} = \binom{12 + 3 - 1}{3 - 1} = \binom{14}{2}
