\[
\mathbf{a} \cdot (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}) = |\mathbf{a}||\mathbf{b}||\mathbf{c}| \sin \phi
\]
where \(\phi\) is the angle between \(\mathbf{a}\) and the vector \(\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}\). Since \(\mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b}, \mathbf{c}\) are unit vectors, this simplifies to:
