This result indicates that regardless of the values of \( a \) and \( b \) chosen uniformly from the interval \( [0, 1] \), the rounding process ensures that the sum of the rounded values \( A \) and \( B \) will always equal the rounded sum \( C \). This reflects the properties of rounding and the uniform distribution of the selected numbers.
