- \(1!! = 1\)
- \(3!! = 3 \times 1 = 3\)
- \(5!! = 5 \times 3 \times 1 = 15\)
- \(7!! = 7 \times 5 \times 3 \times 1 = 105\)

The units digit of a number is the digit in the ones place, which can be found by taking the number modulo 10.

