   \[
   \sin(A + B) = \frac{\tan A + \tan B}{\sqrt{(1 + \tan^2 A)(1 + \tan^2 B)}}
   \]
   and
   \[
   \cos(A + B) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{(1 + \tan^2 A)(1 + \tan^2 B)}},
   \]
   we can express \(\sin(A + B)\) and \(\cos(A + B)\) in terms of \(C\) and \(D\).

