#### Step 5: Calculate Favorable Arrangements
In any arrangement of these 13 cards, the ace of spades can occupy any of the 13 positions. If the ace of spades is in the first position, it is guaranteed to be before all face cards. If it is in the second position, it is still before the face cards if the first position is occupied by a non-face card. 

