   \[
   \tan^3 \theta = x^{3/2}, \quad \tan 3\theta = \frac{3\sqrt{x} - x^{3/2}}{1 - 3x}.
   \]
   Thus,
   \[
   \tan^2 3\theta = \left(\frac{3\sqrt{x} - x^{3/2}}{1 - 3x}\right)^2.
   \]

5. **Calculating \(\tan^2 \theta \tan^2 3\theta\)**:
   We will multiply \(\tan^2 \theta\) and \(\tan^2 3\theta\) together. Given the complexity of the expressions, we can use numerical methods or code to evaluate this product.

