\[
\overrightarrow{BA} = A - B = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 + 5 \\ 4 - 6 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}
\]

#### Step 3.3: Determine the Projection
The projection of \( \overrightarrow{BA} \) onto \( \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \end{pmatrix} \) is given by:
\[
\text{proj}_{\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \end{pmatrix}} \overrightarrow{BA} = \frac{\overrightarrow{BA} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \end{pmatrix}}{\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\ v_2 \end{pmatrix}
\]

