### Approach
To find the multiplicative inverse of \( 160 \) modulo \( 1399 \), we can use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm. The multiplicative inverse exists if and only if \( \gcd(160, 1399) = 1 \). If they are coprime, we can express \( 1 \) as a linear combination of \( 160 \) and \( 1399 \):

\[
